    "updated_at": "2025-11-19T13:27:49Z",
    "body": "Yeah, \"failure\" we need to define as its own type, very similar to how null is defined already.\n\nI think these others we could define in the Booleans section and consider them \"named booleans\" whereby you always have to compare them explicitly (so you don't have to know which is true and which is false). And if we give them `<dfn>`s they can be linked so it's at least explained somewhere.\n\nNot sure who else might have thoughts on this. Maybe @tabatkins or @zcorpan?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
