    "updated_at": "2025-11-19T15:26:14Z",
    "body": "If we require explicit comparison (which I agree sounds correct), then perhaps we shouldn't call them booleans at all but something like \"named return types\"? That heading could explain that these are prose values with no platform representation, and thereby encompass \"failure\" as well as any other widely-used value we came up with?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
