    "created_at": "2025-11-19T18:31:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-19T18:31:22Z",
    "body": "Yes, I think they should be considered and defined as something separate from bools (which are always true/false, or true/false/unknown at worst). I like @mikewest's suggestion. Maybe `<dfn for=return>failure</dfn>` so they're easily linkable with `[=return/failure=]`?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
