    "updated_at": "2025-11-20T07:48:57Z",
    "body": "Lowercase and (optionally?) linked seems good. That goes well with \"continue\" and \"break\". I'm not entirely sure about calling them return types as they can be used as arguments as well (failure certainly is in a few cases).\n\nAlso, if we don't make these be like booleans, what is their type? With booleans it's clear there's two values that go together. If we define all of them like we define null you'd have to always say \"success or failure\", but maybe that's okay? I guess we could do that and null would just be another \"singleton type\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
